| Date       | Payee         | Amount |
| 2024-01-15 | HARRIS TEETER | -45.00 |
Then rows rejected are : CsvRowError
| Line | Reason                        |
| 4    | No date in the Date column    |

Scenario A byte order mark does not become part of the first heading
Description A file saved from a spreadsheet on Windows begins with a BOM. Left
Description in place it makes the first column heading unmatchable, and the
Description error that follows says the Date column is missing, which sends the
Description reader looking in the wrong place.
Given the file begins with a byte order mark and contains
"""
Date,Description,Amount
01/15/2024,HARRIS TEETER,-45.00
"""
Then headings read are : HeadingRead
| Heading     |
| Date        |
| Description |
| Amount      |

DataType Heading
Description One column heading from the header row.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value       | IsValid | Notes                    |
| Date        | true    |                          |
| Description | true    |                          |
|             | false   | An unnamed column        |

