01/15/2024,Harris Teeter,Expenses:Groceries,-45.00
01/16/2024,Shell,Expenses:Auto:Fuel,-52.00
01/17/2024,Unknown,,-10.00
"""
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
When rows imported
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Account                | Amount |
| T1  | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking        | -45.00 |
| T1  | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries     | 45.00  |
| T2  | 2024-01-16 | Shell         | Assets:Checking        | -52.00 |
| T2  | 2024-01-16 | Shell         | Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | 52.00  |
| T3  | 2024-01-17 | Unknown       | Assets:Checking        | -10.00 |
| T3  | 2024-01-17 | Unknown       | Expenses:Uncategorized | 10.00  |
Then accounts created are : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Expenses:Auto      | Expense | true        |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | Expense | false       |

Scenario A category column naming a real account makes a transfer
Description A Quicken export writes a transfer with the other account in square
Description brackets. Stripping them gives the account path, and the result is
Description an ordinary two-posting transfer.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path            | Type | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking | Checking | false       |
| Assets:Savings  | Checking | false       |
Given the csv profile is : CsvProfile Vertical
| Name           | Quicken Export |
| DateColumn     | Date           |
| PayeeColumn    | Payee          |
| CategoryColumn | Category       |
| AmountStyle    | Signed         |
| AmountColumn   | Amount         |
Given the file contains
