# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Duplicates, without an identifier to go on
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DomainTerm Fingerprint : Text
Description The date, amount, and payee of a row taken together, folded to upper
Description case with runs of blanks collapsed. It stands in for the FITID that a
Description CSV file does not have.

BusinessRule How a CSV row is tested against what is already there
Description Weaker than the FITID test of ImportOfx, and it says so: a row that
Description matches is offered rather than skipped, because two genuine visits to
Description one shop on one day for one amount are not rare.
Examples: CsvDispositionRule
| Test | Condition                                                         | Disposition |
| 1    | A posting in this account has the same fingerprint                | Possible    |
| 2    | An uncleared posting in this account has the same amount and check number | Matched |
| 3    | An uncleared posting in this account has the same amount within five days | Matched |
| 4    | Nothing above applies                                             | New         |

Attributes CsvDispositionRule
| Attribute   | Type              | Default |
| Test        | Integer           | 0       |
| Condition   | String            |         |
| Disposition | ImportDisposition | New     |

BusinessRule A row claims at most one transaction already there
Description The tests above ask whether something matching is present. That is
Description not enough, because it answers the same way however many there are.
Description Two rows in one file with the same date, amount and payee are two
Description transactions, not one row read twice, so the file and the book are
Description paired off one for one.
Details Put the other way round: a transaction already in the book can be
Details claimed once. The first matching row claims it; the second finds
Details nothing left and is new. Which of two identical rows does the claiming
Details is not a question, because they are indistinguishable.
Details
Details The test that asks only "is there one like this?" silently loses the
Details second coffee of the day, the second fuel stop, the second identical
Details transfer. Nothing reports it, the register is simply short, and the
Details account reconciles against nothing. Of the two ways to be wrong this
Details is the worse one: an extra row is seen and deleted, a missing row is
Details discovered a year later or never.
Details
Details So the comparison is between two multisets rather than a membership
Details test. The pairing is per account, as every other duplicate test here
Details is, and a claimed transaction is removed from what the next row may
Details claim.
Details
Details The book is never changed to fit the file. Where the book holds more
Details than the file does -- the same amount twice over where the download
Details has it once -- the spare is left alone and nothing is reported about
Details it. The file is a statement of what the bank knows, not an instruction
Details to make the book match.
Examples: ClaimPairing
| InFile | AlreadyThere | Possible | New | Notes                                     |
| 1      | 0            | 0        | 1   | Nothing to claim                          |
| 1      | 1            | 1        | 0   | The one claims the one                    |
| 2      | 0            | 0        | 2   | Two genuine visits, neither seen before   |
| 2      | 1            | 1        | 1   | One claimed; the other is a second visit  |
| 2      | 2            | 2        | 0   | Both claimed                              |
| 3      | 2            | 2        | 1   | Two claimed, one left over                |
| 1      | 2            | 1        | 0   | The spare in the book is left alone        |

Attributes ClaimPairing
| Attribute    | Type    | Default |
| InFile       | Integer | 0       |
| AlreadyThere | Integer | 0       |
| Possible     | Integer | 0       |
| New          | Integer | 0       |
| Notes        | String  | none    |

Scenario Two identical rows against one transaction already there
Description The case the rule exists for, and the one a membership test gets
Description wrong. Two coffees at the same shop on the same day for the same
Description amount, and the book already has one of them.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking        | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee     | Account                | Amount |
| T1  | 2026-03-02 | Joe Coffee | Assets:Checking       | -4.75  |
| T1  | 2026-03-02 | Joe Coffee | Expenses:Uncategorized | 4.75   |
Given the csv profile is : CsvProfile Vertical
| Name           | Quicken Export |
| DateColumn     | Date           |
| PayeeColumn    | Payee          |
| AmountStyle    | Signed         |
| AmountColumn   | Amount         |
Given the file contains
"""
Date,Payee,Amount
03/02/2026,Joe Coffee,-4.75
03/02/2026,Joe Coffee,-4.75
"""
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
When rows imported
Then import summary is : ImportSummary Vertical
| Possible | 1 |
| New      | 1 |
# One row claims the transaction already there and is offered as a possible
# duplicate; the other has nothing left to claim and is new. A membership test
# would have called both of them possible and lost the second coffee.

Scenario Two identical rows with nothing already there are both new
Description The same file into an empty account. Neither row is a duplicate of
Description the other: the file is what the bank says happened.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking        | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
Given the csv profile is : CsvProfile Vertical
| Name           | Quicken Export |
| DateColumn     | Date           |
| PayeeColumn    | Payee          |
| AmountStyle    | Signed         |
| AmountColumn   | Amount         |
Given the file contains
"""
Date,Payee,Amount
03/02/2026,Joe Coffee,-4.75
03/02/2026,Joe Coffee,-4.75
"""
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
When rows imported
Then import summary is : ImportSummary Vertical
| New | 2 |

